---
/**
 * Editorial positioning block.
 * Pulls the strongest lines from the MAZ proposal PDF.
 */
---

<section class="section bg-champagne">
  <div class="container-page">
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.4fr] gap-10 md:gap-20">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why MAZ</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-balance">
          Real analysts, not
          <span class="italic text-moss">set-and-forget</span> software.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6 md:mt-3">
        <p class="text-[1.05rem] md:text-[1.15rem] leading-relaxed">
          Every campaign is managed by a real analyst, every single business
          day. Bids, budgets, placements, search terms, new keyword and ASIN
          opportunities &mdash; reviewed and adjusted in the account, not by a
          bidding algorithm you can&rsquo;t interrogate.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[1.05rem] md:text-[1.15rem] leading-relaxed text-moss">
          You&rsquo;ll know not just <em class="text-ink not-italic underline decoration-gold decoration-2 underline-offset-4">what</em> we changed, but <em class="text-ink not-italic underline decoration-gold decoration-2 underline-offset-4">why</em> we changed it &mdash; documented
          in every update. Major strategy shifts are limited to one or two per
          fortnight so the data stays clean and measurable, and performance is
          judged over realistic 7-14 day windows to account for Amazon&rsquo;s
          attribution lag.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
